  "question": {
    "text": "If <math> <mrow> <mtext>f</mtext><mfenced> <mtext>x</mtext> </mfenced><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn><mtext>x</mtext><mo>−</mo><mi>sin</mi><mtext>x</mtext><mo>,</mo></mrow> </math> <math> <mrow> <mtext>f : R</mtext> <mo>&nbsp;→</mo> <mtext>R</mtext> </mrow> </math> and <math> <mrow> <mtext>g</mtext><mfenced> <mtext>x</mtext> </mfenced><mo>=</mo><msup> <mtext>x</mtext> <mrow> <mfrac> <mn>1</mn> <mn>3</mn> </mfrac> </mrow> </msup> <mo>,</mo></mrow> </math> <math> <mrow> <mtext>g : R</mtext> <mo>&nbsp;→</mo> <mtext>R</mtext> </mrow> </math>, then"
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "text": "both <math> <mtext>f</mtext></math> and <math> <mtext>g</mtext></math> are onto",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>gof</mi></math> is one-one",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "both <math> <mtext>f</mtext></math> and <math> <mtext>g</mtext></math> are one - one",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "All are true",
      "is_correct": true
    }
  ],
  "correct_answer": [
    "D"
  ],
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mtext>f</mtext><mo>'</mo></msup><mfenced><mtext>x</mtext></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>-</mo><mtext>cos x&nbsp;</mtext><mo>∀</mo><mtext>x</mtext><mo>∈</mo><mtext>R⇒</mtext></math>&nbsp; one - one,<br /><br />and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mtext>g</mtext><mo>'</mo></msup><mfenced><mtext>x</mtext></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>3</mn></mfrac><msup><mtext>x</mtext><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></msup><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>⇒</mo></math>one - one<br /><br />Since, both <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">g</mi></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">f</mi></math> are one - one, hence,&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>gof</mi></math> is also one - one.<br /><br />Range of <math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">f</mi><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">x</mi></mrow></mfenced></math> is <math><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mo>-</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">∞</mi><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&nbsp;</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">∞</mi></mrow></mfenced></math> as <math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">f</mi><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">x</mi></mrow></mfenced></math> is continuous and <math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">f</mi><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">x</mi></mrow></mfenced><mo>→</mo><mo>±</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">∞</mi></math> as <math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&nbsp;</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">x</mi><mo>→</mo><mo>±</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">∞</mi></math>.</p><p>Also, since domain of <math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">g</mi><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">x</mi></mrow></mfenced></math> is <math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">R</mi></math>, <math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">y</mi><mo>=</mo><msup><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">x</mi></mrow><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>3</mn></mrow></mfrac></mrow></msup></math><br /><br /><math><mo>⇒</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">x</mi><mo>=</mo><msup><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">y</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>3</mn></mrow></msup></math><br /><br /><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>⇒</mo><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">y</mi><mn>3</mn></msup><mo>∈</mo><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mo>-</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">∞</mi><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&nbsp;</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">∞</mi></mrow></mfenced></math><br /><br /><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>⇒</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">y</mi><mo>∈</mo><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mo>-</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">∞</mi><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&nbsp;</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">∞</mi></mrow></mfenced></math><br /><br /><math><mo>⇒</mo></math> Range of <math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">g</mi><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">x</mi></mrow></mfenced></math> is also <math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">R</mi></math>.<br />&nbsp;</p>"
  }
